  "notes": [
    "Borough is derived from the pickup zone (PULocationID) using the official TLC taxi zone lookup table (taxi_zones/taxi_zone_lookup.csv, downloaded from the TLC public data bucket; the provided taxi_zones/taxi_zones.shp has no accompanying .dbf attribute table, so LocationID->Borough mapping cannot be read from the shapefile alone).",
    "Zones mapped to Unknown/N/A or not present in the lookup are excluded from borough-level aggregation.",
    "Filters applied (inclusive): 0 <= trip_distance <= 100 miles and 0 <= fare_amount <= 1000 USD; rows with null trip_distance / fare_amount / total_amount / PULocationID dropped.",
    "absolute_increase = avg_total_fare(Feb) - avg_total_fare(Jan) of that borough, reported on both monthly rows of the borough; is_max_increase flags the borough with the largest increase.",
    "EWR (Newark Airport) is retained because it is a Borough value in the official lookup; it is not one of the five NYC boroughs and has a very small sample (284 Jan / 279 Feb trips), so its borough-level averages are volatile.",
    "Interpretation: 'largest absolute increase' is taken as the largest positive change in average total fare (Feb - Jan), i.e. an absolute USD increase rather than a percentage change -> Bronx (+$0.80). Sensitivity: if one instead maximises the absolute magnitude of the change regardless of sign, the winner is unstable across filter variants (EWR -$10.65 with the specified inclusive filter, Staten Island -$10.41 when requiring strictly positive fare, Staten Island -$4.67 if EWR is excluded), and those 'winners' are all decreases rather than increases.",
    "Data-quality note: 30 trips in the two files carry a pickup datetime outside their file month (e.g. 2002-12, 2009-01, 2023-12, 2024-03). They were kept (per the task, only distance/fare ranges are filtered) and have no material effect: re-running with an explicit month filter keeps Bronx as the largest increase (+$0.8024).",
    "Trip month is taken from the source file; borough from pickup zone. Average metrics are per-trip means of trip_distance and total_amount."
  ],
  "interpretation": {
    "absolute_increase_definition": "avg_total_fare(Feb) - avg_total_fare(Jan), reported on both monthly rows of the borough",
